00:03:56.990 --> 00:04:00.220
Our status as an independent offensive unit is riding on this.

00:04:00.220 --> 00:04:03.770
Public Security handles the incident, and we handle what caused it.

00:04:03.770 --> 00:04:04.610
Go.

00:05:10.180 --> 00:05:11.740
The enemy just gave the go-ahead.

00:05:12.260 --> 00:05:13.200
Capture them!

00:05:19.300 --> 00:05:20.670
You deserve this...

00:05:21.280 --> 00:05:23.550
Greedy capitalist bastards!

00:05:32.370 --> 00:05:36.310
Today, we've followed the principle of free trade

00:05:36.310 --> 00:05:39.900
to maintain fair prices that will 
spur post-war economic recovery.

00:05:45.760 --> 00:05:48.910
This was his only weapon. Something's fishy.

00:06:05.820 --> 00:06:07.880
The riot squad opened fire?!

00:06:34.280 --> 00:06:36.930
<i>The west team's slaughtering protesters.</i>

00:06:36.930 --> 00:06:38.750
<i>Some are even shooting other cops!</i>

00:06:39.430 --> 00:06:42.000
It's the biggest simultaneous Ghost Hack ever.

00:06:42.000 --> 00:06:44.350
It's crazy, but it's the only explanation.

00:06:45.030 --> 00:06:48.440
There's no tech that'd control 100 people at once.

00:06:48.440 --> 00:06:50.910
The perps on my watch are all dead, too.

00:06:50.910 --> 00:06:54.180
Check the riot squad's lines and find out what caused the attack.

00:06:54.860 --> 00:06:56.960
There's a log that might be Starter's, but...

00:06:56.960 --> 00:06:59.410
Then this isn't hacking. It's a virus.

00:06:59.410 --> 00:07:01.800
I don't see one in the sequence.

00:07:01.800 --> 00:07:04.270
It's a self-destructing Stuxnet-type.

00:07:04.810 --> 00:07:09.740
Someone must be sending packaged
 actions that lets them control groups.

00:07:28.860 --> 00:07:30.130
You, eh?

00:07:38.390 --> 00:07:43.190
I made a deal with the devil for the 
sake of rebuilding and independence!

00:07:43.190 --> 00:07:45.520
Just like you wanted!

00:07:46.450 --> 00:07:53.700
And it invited a second slaughter by water and 
e-money to follow the first slaughter with guns!

00:07:54.100 --> 00:07:57.660
You said cyberbrain tech and the prosthetics industry would build us a future,

00:07:54.460 --> 00:07:56.280
I want a complete media blackout.

00:07:56.280 --> 00:07:57.660
And I mean now!

00:07:57.660 --> 00:08:01.940
but hope wasn't what they brought to Qhardistan!

00:08:01.940 --> 00:08:06.630
They merely sowed the seeds of betrayal that would grow to bleed away my people's pride!

00:08:07.340 --> 00:08:10.550
Have a taste of what that felt like!

00:08:10.550 --> 00:08:13.970
Then you'll have no choice but to grant me asylum!

00:08:14.340 --> 00:08:18.010
Because this is a civilized, pacifist nation!

00:08:18.500 --> 00:08:19.700
Oh, is it?

00:08:57.540 --> 00:08:58.850
Optical camouflage!

00:08:59.900 --> 00:09:02.310
<i>You can't stop Fire-Starter.</i>

00:09:03.830 --> 00:09:05.420
Someone hacked my line?!

00:09:17.780 --> 00:09:18.450
<i>Major?!</i>

00:09:18.830 --> 00:09:19.910
<i>Saito!</i>

00:09:32.460 --> 00:09:33.310
<i>Shit.</i>

00:09:45.630 --> 00:09:47.390
Hello!

00:09:49.980 --> 00:09:51.050
Give me a weapon!

00:09:51.050 --> 00:09:52.270
Okay!

00:09:52.610 --> 00:09:54.240
<i>Major, I'll be right there!</i>

00:09:54.240 --> 00:09:57.450
<i>Don't be stupid. Go after the one who hacked me!</i>

00:10:13.190 --> 00:10:14.370
On your knees!

00:10:15.840 --> 00:10:18.510
Don't resist and I won't shoot you.

00:10:36.490 --> 00:10:37.610
That was outta nowhere!

00:10:38.180 --> 00:10:40.320
This was your job, moron!

00:10:43.410 --> 00:10:45.860
Sorry! That was an accident.

00:10:45.860 --> 00:10:47.800
Equip some handrails!

00:10:50.900 --> 00:10:52.420
<i>Do it, Saito.</i>

00:11:02.540 --> 00:11:04.860
<i>I let him get away. Sorry!</i>

00:11:17.320 --> 00:11:19.450
S{*\fax-0.263}e{*\fax-0.277}c{*\fax-0.29}t{*\fax-0.303}i{*\fax-0.317}o{*\fax-0.33}n {*\fax-0.357}9 {*\fax-0.383}O{*\fax-0.397}f{*\fax-0.41}f{*\fax-0.423}i{*\fax-0.437}ce

00:11:18.440 --> 00:11:19.450
I'm speechless!

00:11:21.250 --> 00:11:25.890
You finally take the job, and then you 
execute someone on the national Net?

00:11:25.890 --> 00:11:26.990
Who, me?

00:11:27.320 --> 00:11:29.130
You have no proof.

00:11:29.130 --> 00:11:31.230
Are you claiming you had no choice?

00:11:31.230 --> 00:11:34.460
You're a super-wizard-class hacker in an ace unit.

00:11:34.460 --> 00:11:38.420
Perhaps the Army was being 
overzealous in their estimate of you.

00:11:39.990 --> 00:11:43.050
Tell me about the virus and that heavy cyborg girl.

00:11:43.050 --> 00:11:45.720
No cyber-virus was detected.

00:11:45.720 --> 00:11:47.840
The girl's name is Tsuda Emma.

00:11:47.840 --> 00:11:52.100
Apparently she's famous on the Net as a game app maker.

00:11:52.100 --> 00:11:54.820
Nine hours after her arrest, and that's all you've got?

00:11:54.820 --> 00:12:01.030
I expected a former Army Special A Rank inspector to surround themselves with more talented subordinates.

00:12:01.340 --> 00:12:06.560
My people's dedicated effort got multiple perps captured alive.

00:12:06.560 --> 00:12:10.330
Wow, great work arresting some mindless packaged drones.

00:12:13.050 --> 00:12:15.710
We could've stopped it if we'd had special authority.

00:12:17.060 --> 00:12:20.330
Then stop playing gangsters and join Section 9.

00:12:21.160 --> 00:12:26.400
Unless you work directly for Home Affairs, you do get official oversight and you don't get secrecy.

00:12:27.330 --> 00:12:29.680
Can you guarantee I'd be able to stay myself?

00:12:30.300 --> 00:12:34.110
Cutting-edge equipment can protect cyberbrains and prosthetic bodies.

00:12:34.110 --> 00:12:36.500
And my Ghost? My beliefs?

00:12:36.500 --> 00:12:39.530
Depends on how skilled you are. I'll even consider a budget.

00:12:41.030 --> 00:12:45.990
Create an international counterterrorist agency for us with the same budget as the Rangers.

00:12:49.360 --> 00:12:51.790
I'm gonna go eat.

00:12:54.380 --> 00:12:56.130
Aramaki, it's been a while.

00:13:00.060 --> 00:13:03.300
Colonel Hozumi. What brings Army intelligence here?

00:13:05.680 --> 00:13:07.710
I'll take the girl from here.

00:13:08.390 --> 00:13:09.640
Care to explain?

00:13:11.260 --> 00:13:14.040
They're from a squad I trust.

00:13:15.500 --> 00:13:20.090
Ex-major Kusanagi Motoko, of the 501.

00:13:20.090 --> 00:13:22.860
Hated your master so much you became a stray, eh?

00:13:23.480 --> 00:13:25.060
Your intel's dated.

00:13:25.060 --> 00:13:26.320
They recreated my rank.

00:13:28.390 --> 00:13:33.040
The cyber-virus used is crucial for us to investigate.

00:13:33.420 --> 00:13:36.280
Explain why it's crucial, please.

00:13:36.280 --> 00:13:41.250
It's a triple package of brainwashing, 
Ghost infiltration, and false memory creation.

00:13:41.660 --> 00:13:42.970
False memory?

00:13:43.750 --> 00:13:48.470
Last I checked, the government doesn't
 admit that's possible, despite all the reports.

00:13:49.720 --> 00:13:54.220
Virus units entered this country via a certain broker.

00:13:54.550 --> 00:13:58.450
Trust me. You won't even manage to indict that girl.

00:13:59.860 --> 00:14:03.560
Unfortunately, she's been transferred to Unit 501.

00:14:03.560 --> 00:14:04.190
When?

00:14:04.580 --> 00:14:07.650
The moment I agreed to their request for cooperation.

00:14:08.380 --> 00:14:11.240
I've never thought you were clever, but this?

00:14:12.050 --> 00:14:15.520
You'll live to regret your stubbornness.

00:14:23.710 --> 00:14:26.240
Terror by false memories...

00:14:27.260 --> 00:14:30.550
Your claims are finally proven, Major.

00:14:30.550 --> 00:14:34.140
So is the existence of a virus that enables Ghost-hacking.

00:14:34.570 --> 00:14:38.100
Here's your next job: escort the girl to Unit 501.

00:14:38.510 --> 00:14:40.810
What? There really was a request?

00:14:40.810 --> 00:14:43.530
Signed by the Defense Minister.

00:14:43.530 --> 00:14:45.750
Now give me one of your men in exchange.

00:14:45.750 --> 00:14:49.200
Did your scary ex-colleague make you want a guard?

00:14:49.200 --> 00:14:51.010
I want information sharing.

00:14:51.010 --> 00:14:52.780
Go renew old workplace friendships.

00:14:53.380 --> 00:14:54.880
Can I ask one thing?

00:14:54.880 --> 00:14:55.750
What is it?

00:14:56.600 --> 00:14:59.000
Assuming I did shoot her...

00:15:00.030 --> 00:15:03.440
why didn't you use my Ghost infiltration key to stop me?

00:15:06.160 --> 00:15:08.720
I can't answer hypothetical questions.

00:15:09.610 --> 00:15:10.350
I see.

00:15:12.720 --> 00:15:16.140
This is Dr. Zhinzhee Bekka Arr Thied, the one the major killed.

00:15:16.740 --> 00:15:20.860
She's Qhardi, but she graduated from
 Kuzan Royal University as valedictorian.

00:15:20.860 --> 00:15:25.610
A big player in Kuzan water importation since the provisional government days.

00:15:26.420 --> 00:15:30.930
But she supported terrorism when she realized the world would forsake her people, eh?

00:15:31.650 --> 00:15:34.590
She's smart and she's got motive, but she's not a hacker.

00:15:35.410 --> 00:15:38.220
Someone else packaged this.

00:15:38.220 --> 00:15:40.500
What about the girl we captured?

00:15:42.120 --> 00:15:45.630
Her name's Tsuda Emma. A 17-year-old war orphan.

00:15:45.630 --> 00:15:49.670
She makes hit cyberbrain games, which she copyrights under the name "Tin Man".

00:15:50.070 --> 00:15:52.920
"Tin Man"... As in <i>The Wizard of Oz</i>?

00:15:52.920 --> 00:15:54.180
What's that?

00:15:54.510 --> 00:16:01.660
In spite of everything, I still believe that people are good at heart, deep down.

00:15:55.170 --> 00:15:59.350
Supposing she's a teenage super-hacker, how does she fit in?

00:15:59.990 --> 00:16:03.090
Don't tell me she's the one you're after?

00:16:01.660 --> 00:16:04.810
I wish to go on living even after my death.

00:16:03.090 --> 00:16:05.810
I'll know when I dive into her Ghost.

00:16:06.250 --> 00:16:08.320
Ishikawa, stay on the virus and the girl.

00:16:08.320 --> 00:16:10.070
Saito, you go to Section 9.

00:16:10.070 --> 00:16:12.480
Paz and Borma, you release the bait.

00:16:12.480 --> 00:16:15.930
Batou, Togusa, and I will escort the girl.

00:16:15.930 --> 00:16:17.530
We're starting round two.

00:16:18.850 --> 00:16:22.990
Suggestion for you, Miss "Hothead Who Charges In Blind".

00:16:24.020 --> 00:16:28.840
How about I become team leader and lead us in a sensible retreat?

00:16:28.840 --> 00:16:31.850
Brave thing to say in my cyberbrain space.

00:16:35.290 --> 00:16:37.760
You want to take this outside?!

00:16:38.190 --> 00:16:41.630
Whoa, knock it off, you guys!

00:17:07.030 --> 00:17:08.840
He's finally on the move.

00:17:08.840 --> 00:17:10.960
Thought I'd die of boredom!

00:17:18.510 --> 00:17:21.180
It might be cool if we could ride in you.

00:17:21.180 --> 00:17:25.450
The major requested a personnel transport shaft from the Maintenance Department!

00:17:25.450 --> 00:17:27.650
Will we pilot you from inside?

00:17:27.650 --> 00:17:29.150
Isn't that our mobile arsenal?

00:17:29.730 --> 00:17:31.200
Where would the weapons go?

00:17:32.440 --> 00:17:34.450
We can just resupply each other.

00:17:34.450 --> 00:17:37.400
If we armed this guy, he could be our backup.

00:17:37.400 --> 00:17:39.400
Backup, eh?

00:17:39.400 --> 00:17:42.900
Why are we using an outdated Logistics model?

00:17:42.900 --> 00:17:47.160
Ape-Face couldn't get the budget the
 major wanted, so he gave us these bots.

00:17:47.870 --> 00:17:51.870
Neurochip-type AIs are hard to hack or infect, anyway.

00:17:51.870 --> 00:17:54.170
So basically, it was us or the junkyard?

00:17:54.580 --> 00:17:55.750
What?

00:17:55.750 --> 00:18:00.830
Not good enough for the ex-cop still wearing a necktie?

00:18:00.830 --> 00:18:05.730
My late father said looking classy shows faith in yourself.

00:18:06.340 --> 00:18:09.690
Watching you, ex-Ranger, I see what he meant.

00:18:10.240 --> 00:18:12.650
Bold words, kid.

00:18:15.740 --> 00:18:20.190
Mr. Batou suggested modifying us so people could ride us!

00:18:20.190 --> 00:18:22.230
I think it's a really great idea!

00:18:22.230 --> 00:18:24.620
What do you think, Major?

00:18:24.950 --> 00:18:26.940
Drop the act.

00:18:27.700 --> 00:18:30.600
I hate machines who pretend to have personalities.

00:18:32.590 --> 00:18:33.410
She's here.

00:18:47.580 --> 00:18:50.790
Did you hack my line to deliberately get yourself caught?

00:18:52.420 --> 00:18:54.480
What is "Fire-Starter"?

00:18:54.480 --> 00:18:56.320
Is it really the name of a hacker?

00:18:57.260 --> 00:18:59.760
Intelligence wants you.

00:18:59.760 --> 00:19:02.280
Military courts don't do plea bargains, you know.

00:19:05.660 --> 00:19:07.750
I smell seawater.

00:19:08.640 --> 00:19:12.230
We aren't even allowed near the sea.

00:19:13.180 --> 00:19:18.340
Programmers are like weapons: 
we're forbidden by law from moving freely.

00:19:18.340 --> 00:19:20.560
So you are the group's hacker.

00:19:20.560 --> 00:19:21.970
What are you after?

00:19:21.970 --> 00:19:27.880
Long ago, glassblowers had no freedom, because glasswork funded the state.

00:19:28.590 --> 00:19:32.690
If they left the country, they were blinded first.

00:19:33.260 --> 00:19:34.530
You're a refugee?

00:19:34.530 --> 00:19:36.150
That's why you started a massacre?

00:19:39.010 --> 00:19:41.930
Do you think cyberbrains make people happy?

00:19:46.820 --> 00:19:49.150
Are your memories trustworthy?

00:19:49.150 --> 00:19:51.790
Or were they planted by someone?

00:19:53.180 --> 00:19:59.810
When micromachine-based cyberization 
came to pass, experts worldwide warned us:

00:19:59.810 --> 00:20:02.900
"False memories will be used to commit crimes."

00:20:03.590 --> 00:20:06.410
Every organization wants that technology.

00:20:06.410 --> 00:20:07.970
My technology.

00:20:08.410 --> 00:20:11.180
You mean you successfully made memory-manipulation tech?

00:20:12.600 --> 00:20:14.900
Your memories might even be...

00:20:17.570 --> 00:20:20.470
I'm diving right here, right now!

00:20:20.470 --> 00:20:21.960
Saw that coming.

00:20:22.680 --> 00:20:25.070
We don't know what this virus is.

00:20:25.070 --> 00:20:26.530
What if you're infected?

00:20:27.500 --> 00:20:30.140
I'll blow it away, and her cyberbrain with it.

00:20:30.140 --> 00:20:35.500
A hacker who commits mass murder
 just to escape deserves assassination.

00:20:35.500 --> 00:20:37.460
During your dive?!

00:20:37.460 --> 00:20:39.960
Your cyber warfare style is twisted.

00:20:40.290 --> 00:20:42.470
I prefer the term "super-wizard-class".

00:20:43.340 --> 00:20:46.120
"Wizard"... Magician.

00:20:46.120 --> 00:20:48.180
The magician who can't go home...

00:20:48.900 --> 00:20:50.890
I'm diving straight in through her line.

00:20:50.890 --> 00:20:52.590
Uh-huh, ignore protocol.

00:20:54.180 --> 00:20:55.850
Hey, something's weird.

00:20:59.020 --> 00:21:00.520
You're being hacked!

00:21:00.520 --> 00:21:02.240
They're doing it through her cyberbrain!

00:21:03.180 --> 00:21:05.660
What's going on? This isn't just backfire!

00:21:06.700 --> 00:21:09.620
Emma... Danger... Emma...

00:21:15.530 --> 00:21:16.510
You...

00:21:25.590 --> 00:21:26.730
Major!

00:21:31.430 --> 00:21:33.600
I'm sorry, Emma...

00:21:33.600 --> 00:21:35.080
I'm sorry.

00:21:35.080 --> 00:21:38.520
It's okay. I wanted this.

00:21:39.080 --> 00:21:40.770
Don't cry, Brinda.

00:21:42.980 --> 00:21:45.720
There are two Ghosts in there?

00:21:55.980 --> 00:21:58.270
I heard about Section 9's meddling.

00:21:59.430 --> 00:22:02.810
You couldn't have shot her before
 she started blabbing about asylum?

00:22:02.810 --> 00:22:06.550
That shooting is currently under investigation, Deputy Director Amagata.

00:22:07.190 --> 00:22:12.000
I can imagine the profound effects this incident will have

00:22:12.000 --> 00:22:16.520
on the Next-Generation Weapons Review Committee you serve on.

00:22:16.520 --> 00:22:19.650
The year-end industry fair has been canceled.

00:22:19.650 --> 00:22:24.790
And thanks to pressure from the Ministry of Foreign Affairs, we won't be unveiling our prototype weapons, either.

00:22:24.790 --> 00:22:27.490
It's shaking the foundations of the company.

00:22:27.990 --> 00:22:33.110
I hear you're pressing for large-scale
 water sales even after Dr. Thied's death.

00:22:33.110 --> 00:22:35.680
I have a duty to fulfill my contract.

00:22:35.680 --> 00:22:39.960
And effective use of resources is
 key for an international company.

00:22:40.480 --> 00:22:43.550
There are some out there who
 can't even secure drinking water.

00:22:44.330 --> 00:22:47.630
If you're here to criticize my economics, I have other work that awaits me.

00:22:55.690 --> 00:22:58.840
You're not cut out for government work.

00:22:58.840 --> 00:23:02.400
Start an NPO and go live in some refugee camp.

00:23:07.320 --> 00:23:09.350
He's annoying.

00:23:09.350 --> 00:23:13.870
He's a classic ex-politician, and he owes me one from my intelligence days.

00:23:13.870 --> 00:23:16.230
Which means he's a reliable source.

00:23:18.020 --> 00:23:21.420
NPOs, camps... and Foreign Affairs?

00:23:22.010 --> 00:23:23.830
The council on weapons development!

00:23:25.170 --> 00:23:28.130
Was that the objective behind the 
cyberterrorism against Harimadara?

00:23:28.660 --> 00:23:34.370
Lately there's a debate about whether next-gen weapons should be produced domestically or developed abroad.

00:23:34.370 --> 00:23:38.870
The overseas faction'd be thrilled if a domestic manufacturer got attacked.

00:23:39.830 --> 00:23:43.950
Here we go: an NPO that "treats cyberization disorders".

00:23:43.950 --> 00:23:49.880
They disseminated cyberization and learning devices in refugee camps in Kuzan during the war.

00:23:49.880 --> 00:23:51.400
And domestically?

00:23:51.400 --> 00:23:55.780
Got a hit on that girl in the same NPO's treatment records.

00:23:55.780 --> 00:23:58.120
Cyberization rejection syndrome.

00:23:58.120 --> 00:24:02.290
Apparently she ran away from a war orphan 
facility because she rejected being cyberized.

00:24:02.690 --> 00:24:05.090
Not wanting a cyberbrain means you're sick?

00:24:05.790 --> 00:24:11.220
The white paper on cyberization the MHLW
 released after the war classifies it with anorexia.

00:24:11.220 --> 00:24:13.180
That's news to me.

00:24:14.280 --> 00:24:17.910
The cyberization business is insanely big money.

00:24:17.910 --> 00:24:23.080
Pretty predictable that people who don't want it get treated as sick.

00:24:23.080 --> 00:24:26.110
Could she be a genuine multiple personality?

00:24:26.110 --> 00:24:30.640
The prevailing theory is that 
personalities split but Ghosts don't.

00:24:31.360 --> 00:24:37.330
The issue is, what did that NPO have to do with a business deal motivated by military development?

00:24:37.730 --> 00:24:41.790
Go at the military-industrial complex from both ends. Soldiers and corporations.

00:24:53.000 --> 00:24:54.240
It's me.

00:24:54.240 --> 00:24:56.300
The others got caught.

00:24:59.880 --> 00:25:03.270
Don't worry, you'll see them in the afterlife.

00:25:08.510 --> 00:25:09.400
Hello!

00:25:10.010 --> 00:25:11.290
Y-You a cop?

00:25:15.980 --> 00:25:18.440
I-I prepared a confession.

00:25:18.440 --> 00:25:19.990
Let me call my lawyer—

00:25:21.190 --> 00:25:23.500
I don't think that's going to happen.

00:25:24.310 --> 00:25:27.070
You killed our bait.

00:25:27.070 --> 00:25:29.460
Better start talking.

00:25:36.020 --> 00:25:38.390
Started to miss your old home?

00:25:40.450 --> 00:25:44.100
I'm only here to bring in your witness, Lt. Col. Kurutsu.

00:25:44.100 --> 00:25:46.140
Tsumugi is standing by.

00:25:46.140 --> 00:25:48.520
Dive if you want to.

00:25:48.520 --> 00:25:50.110
Assuming she has a Ghost, that is.

00:25:51.310 --> 00:25:52.260
What do you mean?

00:25:53.050 --> 00:25:54.660
I'm stepping out.

00:25:54.660 --> 00:25:58.450
As a member of the committee, I need to be at Harimadara's product inspection.

00:25:58.940 --> 00:26:01.610
Still obsessed with your military career?

00:26:02.340 --> 00:26:04.750
At least I didn't run away from it.

00:26:30.690 --> 00:26:32.360
Nice to see you, Kusanagi.

00:26:32.820 --> 00:26:35.700
I didn't think we'd have another chance to work with you.

00:26:35.700 --> 00:26:37.320
Are these your men?

00:26:37.730 --> 00:26:39.770
Yes. Batou and Togusa.

00:26:40.430 --> 00:26:42.270
This is Tsumugi Dokuro.

00:26:42.270 --> 00:26:44.540
They're both cyber warfare tactical officers.

00:26:44.920 --> 00:26:48.810
"Both"? Are they sharing a body?

00:26:48.810 --> 00:26:52.170
She says they're two identical twins in one conjoined body.

00:26:52.170 --> 00:26:55.000
I dunno how they move.

00:26:55.000 --> 00:26:56.510
The world's full of surprises.

00:27:00.150 --> 00:27:02.020
Let's get started.

00:27:11.330 --> 00:27:13.660
So, only the body came back.

00:27:13.660 --> 00:27:14.650
What do you mean?

00:27:15.330 --> 00:27:18.320
She's a technical officer in Lt. Col. Kurutsu's command.

00:27:18.880 --> 00:27:23.040
She was investigating a hacker with
 a special neurochip-type cyberbrain.

00:27:24.060 --> 00:27:25.540
He's known as "Scarecrow",

00:27:25.910 --> 00:27:29.170
and he's a suspect in the terrorist attack on Harimadara.

00:27:29.170 --> 00:27:32.170
Another <i>Oz</i> character?

00:27:32.170 --> 00:27:33.130
Huh?

00:27:33.660 --> 00:27:38.410
Our conclusion is that he's a 
special spy based on postwar tech.

00:27:39.200 --> 00:27:41.770
Emma was the one who reasoned it out.

00:27:41.770 --> 00:27:45.310
She hypothesized a hacker with the same disorder she had.

00:27:45.310 --> 00:27:49.850
Someone who had to incrementally replace his brain with neurochips and prosthetize his body to survive.

00:27:50.270 --> 00:27:52.560
She had that disorder?

00:27:53.260 --> 00:27:57.640
Personality attenuates, and selfhood can't be retained without auxiliary cyberbrains.

00:27:57.640 --> 00:28:03.110
Emma transformed her impairment into her signature trait, as did Scarecrow.

00:28:03.110 --> 00:28:07.960
Emma regularly used advanced cyberization to
 structure her selfhood, but Scarecrow is different.

00:28:08.810 --> 00:28:11.820
To compensate for his attenuated personality, he dubs the Ghosts of others,

00:28:11.820 --> 00:28:14.720
steals their bodies, and assumes their identities.

00:28:14.720 --> 00:28:18.000
Like the scarecrow who can't think
 inserting a false brain into his head.

00:28:18.360 --> 00:28:19.710
Seriously?

00:28:20.140 --> 00:28:22.210
In other words, this is...

00:28:22.210 --> 00:28:23.730
The body is Emma's,

00:28:23.730 --> 00:28:30.460
but it's being operated by a man's brain which is only one-third the normal size and cyberized with neurochips.

00:28:31.380 --> 00:28:35.940
So what I dived into was the girl's dubbed Ghost.

00:28:35.940 --> 00:28:38.400
What happened to her brain?

00:28:38.400 --> 00:28:40.400
Ghost Dubbing would've degraded it.

00:28:40.400 --> 00:28:43.940
It's either in the trash or sliced up in his research lab.

00:28:43.940 --> 00:28:45.370
That's awful...

00:28:46.660 --> 00:28:48.620
Poor Emma.

00:28:48.620 --> 00:28:50.060
I'm sorry.

00:28:50.060 --> 00:28:51.330
It's okay, Junior.

00:28:51.330 --> 00:28:53.000
Don't be afraid.

00:28:53.000 --> 00:28:55.060
I know the lions will come.

00:28:55.060 --> 00:28:56.790
The people with courage...

00:28:56.790 --> 00:28:58.720
Who are you?

00:28:58.720 --> 00:29:00.400
Tell me who you work for.

00:29:00.400 --> 00:29:02.090
I am a scarecrow.

00:29:02.090 --> 00:29:04.190
My brain is fading away.

00:29:04.190 --> 00:29:07.260
I am tin. My heart is fading away.

00:29:07.260 --> 00:29:12.240
Is that Emma talking, or her dubbed Ghost?

00:29:12.240 --> 00:29:15.100
Tin Girl, give me the scarecrow man's name.

00:29:17.650 --> 00:29:20.280
His name is Brinda Jr.

00:29:20.280 --> 00:29:22.320
Please, don't blame him.

00:29:25.420 --> 00:29:27.640
<i>Got a hit at a postwar nursing home!</i>

00:29:27.640 --> 00:29:30.280
<i>And the same NPO is involved with it.</i>

00:29:30.280 --> 00:29:32.270
<i>Brinda Jr., age 32.</i>

00:29:32.270 --> 00:29:35.040
<i>After he was cyberized, he became an accountant at an employment agency.</i>

00:29:35.650 --> 00:29:40.500
<i>His personality's thin, but he memorized a 
200-digit number in two seconds for an IQ test.</i>

00:29:41.150 --> 00:29:43.940
<i>That's textbook for someone with special cognitive abilities.</i>

00:29:43.940 --> 00:29:46.890
<i>Find out which organization set him up as a hacker.</i>

00:29:46.890 --> 00:29:47.810
<i>Roger.</i>

00:29:48.540 --> 00:29:51.270
I'm diving into that man's Ghost.

00:29:52.050 --> 00:29:55.480
There are only a handful of proven double Ghosts in existence.

00:29:55.480 --> 00:29:57.370
We don't know the dangers.

00:29:58.020 --> 00:30:01.170
I want to know which Ghost has motive.

00:30:01.170 --> 00:30:03.940
You're doubting Emma? She's the victim here.

00:30:04.280 --> 00:30:05.830
Then I'll confirm that.

00:30:05.830 --> 00:30:09.410
Batou, be my backup in case they back-hack me.

00:30:09.720 --> 00:30:12.370
Two against two, eh?

00:30:17.050 --> 00:30:19.990
Togusa. Get all the records copied.

00:30:19.990 --> 00:30:21.140
Roger.

00:30:21.140 --> 00:30:24.210
Oh, here... Sorry, it's a call from my dad.

00:30:26.420 --> 00:30:28.390
Hey, Dad, it's been a while.

00:30:28.390 --> 00:30:28.890
Yeah.

00:30:29.190 --> 00:30:31.230
Batou! Restrain Togusa!

00:30:31.900 --> 00:30:34.180
Got it. I'll become the Lion.

00:30:40.280 --> 00:30:41.400
A Mateba, still?

00:30:43.480 --> 00:30:44.550
Don't move!

00:30:57.250 --> 00:30:58.000
Major!

00:30:58.670 --> 00:30:59.410
Let's go.

00:31:02.210 --> 00:31:03.920
<i>This is crazy!</i>

00:31:03.920 --> 00:31:07.340
<i>I found a Starter log on his comm—it's the virus!</i>

00:31:08.170 --> 00:31:12.000
He must have kept the virus inactive within his neurochips.

00:31:12.000 --> 00:31:14.160
His infiltration was unexpectedly quick.

00:31:14.160 --> 00:31:20.690
It combines victims' memories of past hostility with objects in front of them to plant instantaneous false memories?

00:31:51.090 --> 00:31:52.940
Lethal force is a go, right?

00:31:52.940 --> 00:31:55.100
I'll use it on you if you don't start now.

00:31:57.290 --> 00:31:58.680
Who do you think I am?!

00:32:03.100 --> 00:32:06.840
<i>The scarecrow is the virus's host and Togusa's brain is the package, right?</i>

00:32:06.840 --> 00:32:07.320
Yep.

00:32:07.780 --> 00:32:10.470
But the infection route's disturbingly selective.

00:32:10.470 --> 00:32:12.780
Only people around you are being infected.

00:32:14.880 --> 00:32:17.880
<i>Does that mean the onset can be regulated?</i>

00:32:17.880 --> 00:32:21.450
<i>That'd be impossible without a third party to switch it on.</i>

00:32:21.450 --> 00:32:25.250
<i>Which I guess means it's a virus
 whose damage can be controlled.</i>

00:32:25.820 --> 00:32:29.460
<i>Then it's military. Reanalyze yesterday's infection data.</i>

00:32:29.800 --> 00:32:32.750
<i>We don't want to chase the virus; we want to chase the enemy in possession of it.</i>

00:32:33.540 --> 00:32:36.680
I wish to go on living even after my death.

00:32:37.220 --> 00:32:38.390
Hidden data?

00:32:38.390 --> 00:32:44.850
For these 620 reasons, we oppose cyberization without free choice.

00:32:45.460 --> 00:32:53.590
Reason: We submit that software within the 
cyberbrain is vulnerable to third-party tampering.

00:32:54.380 --> 00:32:59.240
Reason: Electronic alteration of memory causes abnormalities

00:32:59.240 --> 00:33:03.540
in the totality of our independent will referred to as the "Ghost".

00:33:04.580 --> 00:33:09.500
Do you actually think a world without infection and infiltration is possible?!

00:33:12.160 --> 00:33:13.420
<i>Tsumugi! You alive?</i>

00:33:14.070 --> 00:33:17.470
<i>I'm running a sim of the scarecrow's brain. Help me.</i>

00:33:17.470 --> 00:33:19.860
<i>You have Tsuda Emma's Ghost infiltration key, don't you?</i>

00:33:19.860 --> 00:33:21.160
<i>Make me a backdoor.</i>

00:33:21.160 --> 00:33:22.360
I see.

00:33:22.360 --> 00:33:26.900
You're going to use Scarecrow's cyberbrain structure to approximate a vaccine?

00:33:39.540 --> 00:33:45.910
Reason: There are currently seventeen possible ways to alter our memories.

00:33:45.910 --> 00:33:47.000
Shit!

00:33:47.570 --> 00:33:51.920
Major! Why won't you use my 
Ghost infiltration key to stop this?!

00:33:51.920 --> 00:33:52.710
It's no use.

00:33:53.260 --> 00:33:54.830
Brinda won't let her.

00:33:55.750 --> 00:33:57.930
I will become anyone.

00:33:57.930 --> 00:34:00.830
I've inputted and erased many Ghosts.

00:34:00.830 --> 00:34:02.800
I disappeared, too...

00:34:02.800 --> 00:34:04.390
Who am I?

00:34:04.390 --> 00:34:07.600
Was Unit 501 a target, too?

00:34:07.600 --> 00:34:09.750
Aren't you a victim after all?!

00:34:10.380 --> 00:34:12.360
There was no other way.

00:34:12.680 --> 00:34:14.250
What are you after?

00:34:29.320 --> 00:34:31.250
Don't disappear, Emma.

00:34:35.030 --> 00:34:38.970
Let's go on living after our deaths, together.

00:34:42.260 --> 00:34:43.390
They're here.

00:34:50.540 --> 00:34:52.150
<i>An attack barrier!</i>

00:34:54.090 --> 00:34:54.860
Major!

00:34:56.050 --> 00:34:56.820
Colonel!

00:34:57.660 --> 00:35:00.370
They fought each other with attack barriers.

00:35:00.370 --> 00:35:02.600
One of them got forwarded.

00:35:02.600 --> 00:35:05.120
I can't believe it was stronger than ours...

00:35:05.120 --> 00:35:07.240
You were infiltrated for a moment.

00:35:07.890 --> 00:35:11.120
Delete all relevant operational 
headquarters from the cyberbrain Net.

00:35:11.120 --> 00:35:13.540
Go after Brinda. There's nothing left to do here.

00:35:18.070 --> 00:35:19.470
Damn stray dog...

00:35:28.100 --> 00:35:30.120
Looks like we pulled it off.

00:35:30.120 --> 00:35:32.540
The host and Starter are still active.

00:35:48.710 --> 00:35:50.870
We can see the ocean, Emma.

00:35:52.980 --> 00:35:55.290
This creeps even me out, Major.

00:35:55.890 --> 00:35:57.230
Report.

00:35:57.230 --> 00:36:01.260
Col. Hozumi from Army intelligence was the one to recruit Brinda Jr.

00:36:01.700 --> 00:36:05.360
"Scarecrow" is an op cooked up by their old Investigations Section

00:36:05.360 --> 00:36:08.840
during a period when they were working on Ghost Dub devices.

00:36:08.840 --> 00:36:13.760
Hozumi got on the Next-Gen Weapons
 Review Committee through Foreign Affairs.

00:36:14.540 --> 00:36:22.490
But she wasn't there long, and Kurutsu of Unit 501 took her seat at Vice-Minister Kitahara's recommendation.

00:36:23.220 --> 00:36:27.950
Unit 501 got a hold on Hozumi 
through military musical chairs, eh?

00:36:27.950 --> 00:36:39.670
Reason: We can prove that false memories compel us to commit murder, suicide, and other criminal acts.

00:36:37.770 --> 00:36:39.670
Which one built the pod?

00:36:40.050 --> 00:36:41.300
Unknown.

00:36:41.300 --> 00:36:45.650
But Army intelligence decided to rally by interfering with the Review Committee.

00:36:46.470 --> 00:36:49.880
I'd guess that somewhere in there, 
the two hackers became aware of each other.

00:36:49.880 --> 00:36:52.970
The attack on Harimadara is the connection?

00:36:52.970 --> 00:36:55.840
There's no evidence they did it.

00:36:55.840 --> 00:37:01.610
But Hozumi is in the overseas weapons development faction, and Harimadara's a domestic faction stronghold.

00:37:02.280 --> 00:37:04.070
Who shot our bait?

00:37:04.070 --> 00:37:07.200
A Kuzan water cartel hit man.

00:37:07.200 --> 00:37:10.540
Hozumi's playing with serious fire.

00:37:10.540 --> 00:37:16.610
She used the pretext of wartime industry to interfere in Kuzan's affairs while she was stationed there during the war.

00:37:16.610 --> 00:37:21.130
If she can't subdue the domestic faction and give the cartel the profits she promised,

00:37:21.130 --> 00:37:23.720
it'll retaliate against her.

00:37:23.720 --> 00:37:25.450
Starter analysis results?

00:37:25.450 --> 00:37:30.560
Couldn't pin down the trigger, but I got 
my answer from the fact that we couldn't

00:37:31.060 --> 00:37:35.630
find the infection route into the building even though Section 9 had domination over it.

00:37:35.630 --> 00:37:38.360
It was a C4ISR network.

00:37:38.360 --> 00:37:40.520
A military communications system.

00:37:40.520 --> 00:37:42.690
Things are starting to become clear.

00:37:42.690 --> 00:37:49.240
Col. Hozumi's the one who activated Starter and patched the virus through to infect the VIP room's security.

00:37:49.700 --> 00:37:52.050
She was after the woman the guard shot.

00:37:52.050 --> 00:37:55.210
Senior Vice-Minister Kitahara, 
who's with the domestic faction.

00:37:55.580 --> 00:37:58.520
That massacre was a smokescreen for one murder?!

00:37:58.520 --> 00:38:00.420
Guess she's a born war-lover.

00:38:00.780 --> 00:38:03.200
Why snipe Tin Girl?

00:38:03.200 --> 00:38:03.880
That was a bluff.

00:38:04.300 --> 00:38:08.950
She must've wanted to get rid of us and get Tin Girl safely to the 501.

00:38:09.580 --> 00:38:12.610
So her little visit to Section 9 was a smokescreen, too?

00:38:12.610 --> 00:38:16.600
She backed down so easily because 
she was after Unit 501 from the start.

00:38:16.980 --> 00:38:21.570
So she could set up anti-cyberbrainist 
Tsuda Emma as the massacre's ringleader.

00:38:21.570 --> 00:38:25.240
Harimadara, the Vice-Minister, the 501...

00:38:25.240 --> 00:38:28.170
She had a threefold plan to take them all out!

00:38:28.170 --> 00:38:30.430
What about the Ghost of the girl who got dubbed?

00:38:30.430 --> 00:38:35.400
If she does have her own will, why'd she knowingly let Hozumi use her?

00:38:35.400 --> 00:38:40.520
Just from the circumstances, 
the scarecrow is the one you've been after.

00:38:40.520 --> 00:38:42.880
He didn't necessarily write the virus.

00:38:42.880 --> 00:38:45.010
Hozumi said there was a broker.

00:38:45.430 --> 00:38:48.960
If she told the truth, someone out there made and sold it.

00:38:48.960 --> 00:38:50.470
That's who I'm after.

00:38:50.470 --> 00:38:52.360
This is all speculation.

00:38:52.360 --> 00:38:56.820
Right now, there's only one way for us to get proof.

00:38:56.820 --> 00:38:58.900
I assume you have Togusa's location.

00:38:58.900 --> 00:39:00.320
We'll meet en route.

00:39:00.320 --> 00:39:04.190
We're going to capture both Ghosts—
the scarecrow's, and the girl's.

00:39:05.190 --> 00:39:06.930
Togusa's the problem.

00:39:06.930 --> 00:39:10.700
Blowing a married teammate's brains out ain't my job.

00:39:11.210 --> 00:39:14.330
We know for sure this infection plants false memories, right?

00:39:14.330 --> 00:39:17.370
You saw him talking to his dead father.

00:39:18.060 --> 00:39:19.960
There should be a shared form.

00:39:19.960 --> 00:39:24.470
I'll get infected, so you ID it and 
version up your makeshift vaccine.

00:39:24.470 --> 00:39:26.420
You want to mirror your own brain?

00:39:26.420 --> 00:39:29.340
Worst case scenario, blow my brains out.

00:39:29.340 --> 00:39:31.530
So that's my job?

00:39:31.530 --> 00:39:34.340
You can always let me be the leader, you know.

00:39:35.180 --> 00:39:35.810
A checkpoint?

00:39:38.220 --> 00:39:40.900
You're on the wanted list as a suspected terrorist!

00:39:40.900 --> 00:39:42.580
Shit, it's Section 9!

00:39:42.580 --> 00:39:44.700
The ape used to be in Army intelligence.

00:39:44.700 --> 00:39:47.230
He cut a deal with Hozumi, and he's framing us!

00:39:47.700 --> 00:39:49.760
She may just want us to think so.

00:39:49.760 --> 00:39:52.200
I'll send Section 9 our intel.

00:39:52.620 --> 00:39:55.040
After all this, you're still relying on him?!

00:39:55.040 --> 00:39:56.050
No.

00:39:56.050 --> 00:39:56.870
Why, then?!

00:39:58.020 --> 00:40:00.750
It's something my Ghost is whispering to do.

00:40:17.600 --> 00:40:18.680
Wait!

00:40:18.680 --> 00:40:20.060
Where are you going?!

00:40:21.610 --> 00:40:23.020
Stop!

00:40:24.300 --> 00:40:26.730
We promised we'd go far away.

00:40:33.860 --> 00:40:34.960
Goodbye.

00:40:56.610 --> 00:40:58.260
I released the package!

00:41:00.500 --> 00:41:01.620
I'm going on ahead.

00:41:02.690 --> 00:41:04.760
I told you to shoot if things went south!

00:41:04.760 --> 00:41:06.150
Take a damn gun with you...

00:41:08.800 --> 00:41:09.790
Major...

00:41:13.590 --> 00:41:15.320
She's in pieces!

00:41:15.320 --> 00:41:17.530
If she's a neurochip version, she's still alive.

00:41:21.010 --> 00:41:23.160
We'll go on living.

00:41:32.560 --> 00:41:35.680
It's a Ghost Dub, not a transfer?!

00:41:45.600 --> 00:41:47.400
That's a Harimadara prototype!

00:41:50.820 --> 00:41:52.100
Major!

00:41:52.100 --> 00:41:54.760
Two Ghosts have been dubbed into that thing.

00:41:54.760 --> 00:41:57.750
We're going to stop it! Logicomas, give me everything you've got!

00:41:57.750 --> 00:41:59.280
Yes, sir!

00:42:02.200 --> 00:42:05.660
Where the hell would they abandon their own lives to go?

00:42:07.290 --> 00:42:08.130
The ocean.

00:42:08.680 --> 00:42:09.330
Huh?

00:42:09.810 --> 00:42:11.530
They're not going anywhere!

00:42:11.530 --> 00:42:12.840
This ends here!

00:42:58.720 --> 00:43:02.160
Next-gen weapon or not, its brains are rookies.

00:43:02.160 --> 00:43:04.180
Aim for the eyes and legs, and it's in the bag.

00:43:18.030 --> 00:43:19.240
For real?!

00:44:08.930 --> 00:44:10.080
Got you now!

00:44:21.680 --> 00:44:22.970
What's that?

00:44:22.970 --> 00:44:26.140
It's Army intelligence! The bastards requested an artillery strike!

00:44:33.340 --> 00:44:35.550
You've cut off your sensory system?!

00:44:36.260 --> 00:44:37.020
Crap!

00:44:46.450 --> 00:44:48.720
You discarded intensity regions...

00:44:48.720 --> 00:44:53.510
Recognition systems, memory fields, 
the Net that maintains your architecture...

00:45:14.540 --> 00:45:17.250
You even jettisoned your own Ghost!

00:45:17.250 --> 00:45:20.360
You want a life you've stripped all meaning from?!

00:46:35.680 --> 00:46:36.580
Goodbye.

00:47:05.420 --> 00:47:07.120
It's over.

00:47:07.120 --> 00:47:10.390
Return to base. We're going to Kuzan, by way of Benares.

00:47:13.340 --> 00:47:16.720
The world's cyber economy has only just begun.

00:47:16.720 --> 00:47:19.060
I'll pay whatever it takes to reconcile with the cartel—

00:47:32.070 --> 00:47:33.450
On your knees, hands in the air!

00:47:35.340 --> 00:47:37.270
Oh, the wanted poster.

00:47:37.270 --> 00:47:38.410
Told you so.

00:47:46.490 --> 00:47:48.770
You're just like that Section 9 chief.

00:47:48.770 --> 00:47:52.480
Never happy unless you're digging up what's dead and buried.

00:47:53.610 --> 00:47:56.070
It's something you ran away without doing.

00:47:58.350 --> 00:48:01.520
Nothing's going to change, Kusanagi.

00:48:02.580 --> 00:48:05.000
We're an independent offensive unit.

00:48:05.810 --> 00:48:11.490
We stand independent of the system, and we have
 truly discrete personalities that don't get packaged.

00:48:12.210 --> 00:48:15.400
When we're officially approved as top priority,

00:48:15.400 --> 00:48:19.450
we'll root out all the sorry bastards who 
conspire because they're afraid of a scandal.

00:48:21.960 --> 00:48:24.490
And you count me as one of them?

00:48:26.380 --> 00:48:29.310
I never changed your channel.

00:48:29.310 --> 00:48:32.690
Contact me whenever you want to come home.

00:48:45.540 --> 00:48:46.860
You're free to go.

00:48:46.860 --> 00:48:49.940
We voided the wanted notice Col. Hozumi put out.

00:48:50.500 --> 00:48:54.530
Vice-Minister of Defense Kitahara wants to thank you.

00:48:54.530 --> 00:48:56.410
Is that some sort of joke?

00:48:57.030 --> 00:48:58.620
A political one.

00:48:59.260 --> 00:49:02.640
Section 9 just went through Col. Hozumi's possessions

00:49:02.640 --> 00:49:07.190
and confiscated a Ghost Dub device and an outline of the Scarecrow op.

00:49:07.190 --> 00:49:09.460
They couldn't arrest her, though.

00:49:09.460 --> 00:49:11.840
No—but then she confessed.

00:49:16.110 --> 00:49:20.230
Her chopper was shot down with Kuzan weapons.

00:49:21.120 --> 00:49:26.790
She's afraid enough of the cartel's revenge to 
request protective custody and a plea bargain.

00:49:26.790 --> 00:49:28.760
So she'll get let off scot-free.

00:49:28.760 --> 00:49:30.390
I'll make sure she doesn't.

00:49:30.390 --> 00:49:35.280
The NPO she worked with is a 
front for dirty cyberbrain business.

00:49:35.280 --> 00:49:40.370
Not only that, we've detected Starter in her cyberbrain, just like your intel said.

00:49:41.140 --> 00:49:44.680
She got a lot of people injured or killed, and I'll make her pay for that—

00:49:44.680 --> 00:49:47.430
even if I can't take her to court yet.

00:49:48.380 --> 00:49:50.720
Where did she get the virus?

00:49:50.720 --> 00:49:53.420
Through a broker, she says.

00:49:53.420 --> 00:49:56.240
She claims to know nothing about its author.

00:49:56.240 --> 00:49:57.090
I see.

00:49:58.370 --> 00:50:01.060
Was it really the cartel who tried to kill Hozumi?

00:50:01.860 --> 00:50:05.790
Even if it was someone who wanted to prevent us from investigating her,

00:50:05.790 --> 00:50:08.020
I'm sure any trace of them is long gone.

00:50:21.290 --> 00:50:22.410
Major.

00:50:22.730 --> 00:50:25.080
All of you came?

00:50:25.080 --> 00:50:27.870
I didn't know I had such admirable subordinates.

00:50:28.170 --> 00:50:31.130
You could've been attacked while in custody.

00:50:31.790 --> 00:50:34.550
We've been keeping an eye on all the suspicious cats passing by.

00:50:36.000 --> 00:50:37.520
One more thing.

00:50:37.520 --> 00:50:42.270
I told the Minister of Home Affairs that your team contributed to deterring the virus.

00:50:43.100 --> 00:50:48.020
Use your vaunted cyberbrain to read
 Public Security Commission report N2077.

00:50:48.540 --> 00:50:51.990
As of tomorrow, you get special authority.

00:50:51.990 --> 00:50:53.980
Without official oversight.

00:50:54.700 --> 00:50:56.970
This case isn't over.

00:50:56.970 --> 00:51:01.000
Investigate the high-level hacking 
virus and any organizations involved,

00:51:01.740 --> 00:51:04.380
and plan to attend plenty of funerals along the way.

00:51:04.380 --> 00:51:06.450
I shot Thied.

00:51:07.180 --> 00:51:09.710
You must've had a hunch that an 
intelligence bigwig was behind this,

00:51:10.030 --> 00:51:13.050
meaning you would've wanted an intel advantage at any cost.

00:51:13.050 --> 00:51:15.210
So why didn't you stop me?!

00:51:16.150 --> 00:51:19.460
Because I don't have your Ghost infiltration key.

00:51:22.560 --> 00:51:25.810
No organization will ever have it.

00:51:26.570 --> 00:51:30.020
I promised your late commander that.

00:51:54.680 --> 00:52:00.420
Bottom line, all we figured out was that someone out there

00:52:00.420 --> 00:52:04.350
used a couple of anti-cyberbrainist hackers and a miserable water company chick.

00:52:05.060 --> 00:52:08.160
We may be looking for a crime worth sacrificing lives over,

00:52:08.160 --> 00:52:13.720
but all we have are money-mad war profiteers and a man and girl obsessed with casting things away.

00:52:13.720 --> 00:52:15.080
For now, that is.

00:52:16.830 --> 00:52:21.330
Which one had agency, the man or the girl?

00:52:21.330 --> 00:52:24.620
Did they even have real will?

00:52:26.210 --> 00:52:29.360
When they blocked my infiltration, at least.

00:52:30.190 --> 00:52:36.050
But they fled with nowhere to go, 
then had to transfer into that weapon.

00:52:36.590 --> 00:52:41.620
That think-tank's cyberbrain had a massive output system.

00:52:41.620 --> 00:52:42.350
Hmm?

00:52:43.060 --> 00:52:50.310
What if the reason they cast away what made them themselves was to output the last thing left into the Net?

00:52:50.710 --> 00:52:53.110
You think that's where they were going?

00:52:53.110 --> 00:52:57.840
Pouring the last shreds of their Ghosts into the Net... Is that even possible?

00:52:59.240 --> 00:53:02.460
It's been researched, but it's impossible to prove.

00:53:05.290 --> 00:53:10.060
But in the moment their Ghosts were lost,
 I got the feeling they'd fused.

00:53:10.060 --> 00:53:11.910
That two lives had become one...

00:53:12.880 --> 00:53:14.560
That isn't like you.

00:53:14.560 --> 00:53:18.160
Ghosts are the most independent things in this world.

00:53:18.160 --> 00:53:22.460
Even the ones being controlled are
 fundamentally, eternally standalone.

00:53:22.460 --> 00:53:24.190
Like our squad, yeah?

00:53:27.990 --> 00:53:29.350
Yeah.

00:53:29.820 --> 00:53:32.500
Well? The floaters are all ready.

00:53:32.500 --> 00:53:34.720
I got a set of two.

00:53:34.720 --> 00:53:37.560
Even someone with a titanium skull wouldn't drown.

00:53:37.560 --> 00:53:40.640
You seriously want to swim in the ocean in midwinter?

00:53:40.640 --> 00:53:43.320
Gotta shake off those memories of almost drowning.

00:53:43.820 --> 00:53:46.680
Plus it ain't too often I get to see you in a swimsuit.

00:53:46.680 --> 00:53:48.170
That's your real goal?

00:53:48.170 --> 00:53:48.910
Huh?

00:53:48.910 --> 00:53:49.960
Unbelievable.

00:53:49.960 --> 00:53:53.250
No, no! I'm doing this all for you!

00:53:55.800 --> 00:53:57.610
I'll take a rain check.

00:53:57.610 --> 00:53:59.930
No, just—you got it all wrong!

00:54:31.440 --> 00:54:38.230
yureru kanashimi soshite nikushimi

00:54:31.440 --> 00:54:38.230
Our vague sadness and our hate

00:54:38.230 --> 00:54:43.030
minna kasun de iku

00:54:38.230 --> 00:54:43.030
fades away

00:54:43.610 --> 00:54:48.640
kishin da {(spirits)}

00:54:43.610 --> 00:54:48.640
and we split.

00:54:48.640 --> 00:54:50.210
We're taking,

00:54:50.210 --> 00:54:52.560
We're taking a way

00:54:55.010 --> 00:54:56.720
A way

00:54:57.930 --> 00:55:01.220
togire ta memory

00:54:57.930 --> 00:55:01.220
Troubled memories

00:55:01.220 --> 00:55:04.640
sora ni koritsuku

00:55:01.220 --> 00:55:04.640
frozen in the sky.

00:55:04.640 --> 00:55:09.520
sake ta kono kokoro ga

00:55:04.640 --> 00:55:09.520
This torn heart is

00:55:10.120 --> 00:55:14.190
futatsu ni

00:55:10.120 --> 00:55:14.190
splitting

00:55:12.290 --> 00:55:18.520
splitting

00:55:12.290 --> 00:55:18.520
in two.

00:55:15.120 --> 00:55:16.680
We're making,

00:55:16.680 --> 00:55:18.900
We're making a way

00:55:21.490 --> 00:55:23.200
nowhere.

00:55:23.200 --> 00:55:28.330
We split in two.

00:55:28.330 --> 00:55:29.810
We're slipping,

00:55:29.810 --> 00:55:32.540
We're slipping away

00:55:34.710 --> 00:55:36.910
No way home.

00:55:44.640 --> 00:55:45.820
Ghost,

00:56:03.110 --> 00:56:11.070
kowareta spirits

00:56:03.110 --> 00:56:11.070
Our spirit is broken.

00:56:08.010 --> 00:56:09.680
We're breaking,

00:56:09.680 --> 00:56:12.200
We're breaking away.

00:56:14.500 --> 00:56:16.140
Away

00:56:16.140 --> 00:56:21.280
kieteku slipping

00:56:16.140 --> 00:56:21.280
We're disappearing.

00:56:21.280 --> 00:56:22.830
We're going,

00:56:22.830 --> 00:56:25.430
We're going insane.

00:56:27.690 --> 00:56:29.160
No way.

00:56:30.520 --> 00:56:37.390
kiri hana sareta tamashii tachi wa

00:56:30.520 --> 00:56:37.390
I shed all my mistakes,

00:56:37.390 --> 00:56:38.870
nemuru

00:56:37.390 --> 00:56:38.870
and now

00:56:39.520 --> 00:56:42.610
yume mo mire zu

00:56:39.520 --> 00:56:42.610
they sleep dreamlessly,

00:56:42.610 --> 00:56:45.650
samayou

00:56:42.610 --> 00:56:45.650
